---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import { BRANDS, SITE, DIRECTORY_URL } from '../lib/site';
import { breadcrumbNode } from '../lib/schema';

const pageUrl = `${SITE.url}/about/`;
const crumbs = [{ label: 'Home', href: '/' }, { label: 'About' }];
const schema = [
  breadcrumbNode(crumbs, pageUrl),
  { '@type': 'AboutPage', '@id': `${pageUrl}#page`, url: pageUrl, name: 'About Relocado', about: { '@id': `${SITE.url}/#organization` } },
];
---
<BaseLayout
  title="About Relocado: Who Writes It and How It Works"
  description="Who runs Relocado, how the guides are researched and checked, how the directory is compiled, and how the site links to its sister businesses."
  schema={schema}
>
  <div class="page-header">
    <div class="wrap">
      <Breadcrumbs items={crumbs} />
      <span class="kicker">About</span>
      <h1>About Relocado</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        A practical guide to moving in or out of Singapore: what to do, in what order, and by when.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="wrap">
    <article class="prose prose-narrow">
      <h2>Who runs it</h2>
      <p>
        Relocado is run by the team behind three Singapore businesses. Junk to Clear was established in 2009
        under SKAP Waste Management Pte. Ltd., and HomeToMoved and HomeToClean are run by the same team.
      </p>
      <ul>
        {BRANDS.map((b) => (
          <li><a href={b.url}>{b.name}</a>: {b.does}</li>
        ))}
      </ul>
      <p>
        Junk to Clear clears homes for people leaving Singapore. Relocado covers the rest of that move: the
        paperwork, the lease, the shipment and the timing.
      </p>

      <h2>How we link to our own businesses</h2>
      <p>
        A guide links to one of the three businesses only at a step that needs that service, such as
        clearing a flat before handover, and the sentence says it’s ours. Guides never rank or review our own
        businesses against anyone else’s. Relocado doesn’t ship anything overseas, so for international moves
        we point to other companies.
      </p>

      <h2>How the guides are researched</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Rules, deadlines and eligibility come from the official source (IRAS, MOM, CPF Board, LTA, ICA, Singapore Customs, NEA, HDB and others), which each guide lists and links to.</li>
        <li>Where something depends on your contract rather than the law, such as a diplomatic clause, we say so and tell you to check your agreement.</li>
        <li>We don’t publish prices, statistics or claims we can’t source.</li>
        <li>Each guide shows the date it was last checked. Rules change, and if a source says something different from a guide, the source is right.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Guides are general information, not legal, tax or immigration advice.</p>

      <h2>How the directory works</h2>
      <p>
        The <a href={DIRECTORY_URL}>directory</a> lists Singapore international movers, relocation companies
        and pet relocation specialists: the parts of a move our own businesses don’t do. Each entry comes from
        the company’s own website and shows the date it was checked. The listings are alphabetical and aren’t
        a ranking, and nobody pays to appear. If you run a listed company and something is wrong, or you’d
        like to be removed, email us.
      </p>

      <h2 id="privacy">Privacy</h2>
      <p>
        Relocado uses Google Analytics to count visits and see which guides help people. It records the pages
        you view, how you arrived (from a search, for example), how far you scroll, which links to other sites
        you click, and your device, browser and approximate location. It uses first-party cookies to tell
        visits apart. It doesn’t collect your name or email address, and Google Analytics doesn’t log or store
        IP addresses. Google keeps the data for 14 months. You can opt out on any site with
        <a href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout" rel="noopener">Google’s opt-out browser add-on</a>.
      </p>
      <p>
        The <a href="/leaving-singapore/planner/">leaving Singapore planner</a> keeps the dates you enter in your
        own browser, and nothing you type into it is sent to us. If you email us, we use your address only to reply.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Corrections, questions and directory changes: <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>.
      </p>
    </article>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
